What this project changes
-------------------------

Nothing in the CorridorKey code or model. This repository does not contain
or modify any CorridorKey source files or weights. It adds:

- Dockerfile: builds a RunPod serverless image that fetches CorridorKey 2.0
  at a pinned commit and downloads the weights with upstream's own
  scripts/download_weights.py at build time.
- worker/handler.py: a RunPod job handler that calls upstream's
  load_model() and run_inference() (from corridorkey/runtime.py), moves
  files to and from presigned URLs, and reports timings.
- ckremote.py: a client that uploads a clip to the user's own bucket, runs
  the job on the user's own RunPod endpoint and records timings.

Nobody running this project pays us anything. Users pay RunPod and their
storage provider directly, with their own accounts.

Third-party components are listed in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.
